Here's MediCore Companion v3 — all five missing flows are now built in. Here's exactly what was added:

🔴 Doctor Escalation Inbox — a full dedicated tab (with a live red badge showing 3 active) showing escalations from nurses with severity levels, SLA countdown timers that pulse red when under 5 minutes, vitals recorded at time of escalation, an AI CDSS suggestion grounded on the finding, a list of suggested actions, and Acknowledge / Mark Resolved buttons. Tap any escalation to drill into its full detail screen.
🔔 Nurse → Doctor Escalation Send — every escalatable task in the nurse worklist now has an orange "Escalate" button. Tapping it slides up a panel where the nurse picks severity (CRITICAL / HIGH / MED), selects the doctor to notify, types the clinical finding, and hits Send. A confirmation screen confirms the SLA timer has started and the audit trail is created. ESI-2 triage patients also get an Escalate button directly on the triage card.
💬 Secure Messaging — a full messaging inbox for both Doctor and Nurse, showing threads categorised by type (message, task, escalation, consultation, alert, referral) with priority badges and unread counts. Tap a thread to open the full conversation with a send input. Compose new message flow with recipient, patient context, type picker, and message body. Encrypted + HIPAA audit trail shown throughout.
💊 Medication Reminders — each medication card shows the 7-day adherence dot grid (Mon–Sun), a reminder toggle that turns the bell on/off, a "Mark as Taken" button that animates to a confirmation, and the key safety note for that drug. An AI adherence summary card shows the weekly score. The home screen also has a medication reminder strip that deep-links here.
💳 Mobile Bill Payment — outstanding invoices with line-item breakdown, a 3-step payment flow: choose method → review → confirmed. Payment methods include EcoCash (with Econet red branding), OneMoney (green), card, and bank transfer. Pending medical aid claims (CIMAS) show their status inline. The home screen quick actions button routes straight here.
🔔 Notification Centre — a bell in the status bar with a live unread badge. Tapping opens a full notification screen with category filter chips (all, escalation, message, result, reminder, bill). Each notification deep-links to the right screen when tapped. Completely role-specific — doctors see escalations and PostVisit alerts, nurses see task reminders and acknowledgements, patients see medication reminders and bill notifications.